; Thorin asks where the thief is
;
; Script handler (op 3, in Thorin's script #R$C8FF). When Thorin is where the
; player is and the player is invisible (the present/visible flag, bit 7 of
; the player's flags, is cleared while the ring is worn, #R$A377) he says
; "Where's the thief ?". Otherwise it returns before the test pass accepts,
; so the script takes its alternative step (#R$C90C, #R$A657).
; .
; Hardware: none (the text goes through the message printer).
@label=ThorinMissesThief
c$A640 LD A,($B6F6)  ; location of the NPC being run
 $A643 LD HL,$B6F5
 $A646 CP (HL)
 $A647 RET NZ        ; not with the player: refuse
 $A648 LD A,($C122)  ; the player's flags
@isub=BIT FLAG_PRESENT,A
 $A64B BIT 7,A
 $A64D RET NZ        ; visible: refuse
 $A64E CALL $9D44
 $A651 LD HL,$B0CB   ; "Where's the thief ?"
 $A654 JP $A1E3
